From 69fd99dea0bedc12d30c8e9659db8c3dd6a20746 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:19:58 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Markdown images in replies: any local folder, kept when the
 reply finishes

An image a reply names in Markdown (`![alt](path)`) showed only when the
file sat inside the chat's own folder, was read live from the file each
time, and a relative path in a projectless (scratch) chat stayed a link.
Agents reached for show_image instead: one tool call per picture.

- engine/reply_images.rs (new): a reply's image paths resolve on the
  chat's host from any local folder: absolute, `~/...`, or relative to
  the chat's folder. Still refused: URLs, network (UNC) and device paths,
  and a link that leads to one (each component is lstat'ed; links to
  local paths are followed). Only PNG/JPEG/WebP/GIF by extension and
  first bytes, at most 10 MB.
- When a reply segment finishes, the host copies each image it names (up
  to 8) to {uploads}/reply-images/, named by chat and resolved path, so
  it outlives its file. Same name every time: a replay or restart
  rewrites, never adds. ReadChatImageChunk serves that copy first, else
  the file.
- rpc.rs: the chat's folder only joins relative paths now; the host
  check (only the chat's host answers) stays.
- ui/reply_images.rs: `~/...` and relative paths the UI can't expand (a
  scratch chat's `~/.zeron/scratch/...` folder) go to the host as
  written.
- mcp: the instructions tell agents to show an image file as a Markdown
  image; show_image stays available.

Tests: engine reply_images (4), uploads (15), rpc chat_image (1), e2e
chat_images_come_from_any_folder_of_their_chats_host and
a_finished_replys_images_outlive_their_files, zeron-mcp (59).
